{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1250,1445p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1940,2075p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1270,1425p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '535,565p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"      (pos? o) (assoc :origins o))))\n\n\n(defn- link-raise\n  \"The raise of a resumed link wait, carrying the identity the parked\n   evaluation has minted so far -- the counters of the VM the raise\n   interrupted, whose every earlier run is in them -- so a rollback\n   cannot reuse it.  It carries the query interpreter's pair too: the\n   requests it has answered stay answered when the shell rolls back.\n   So are the admission state and the in-process admission\n   interpreter's, as they stand after the serve that answered: a\n   question the raise settled is not asked or answered again.\"\n  [error vm state]\n  (ex-info (or (ex-message error) \"Link failed\")\n           (assoc (or (ex-data error) {})\n                  ::link-counter (:id-counter vm)\n                  ::link-origins (:origins vm)\n                  ::query-pair (:query-pair state)\n                  ::link-pair (:link-pair state)\n                  ::admission (:admission state)\n                  ::admitter (:admitter state)\n                  ::dht (:dht state)\n                  ::indexer (:indexer state))))\n\n\n(defn- carry-served\n  \"`state` rolled back by a link raise, keeping what the interpreters\n   already concluded: the query pair, the link pair past every request\n   answered, the admission state and its interpreter's past every\n   question settled, the DHT node a load started or forgot on, and the\n   indexer a `yin.link/publish` committed its name envelopes through.\"\n  [state d]\n  (cond-> state\n    (::query-pair d) (assoc :query-pair (::query-pair d))\n    (::link-pair d) (assoc :link-pair (::link-pair d))\n    (::admission d) (assoc :admission (::admission d))\n    (::admitter d) (assoc :admitter (::admitter d))\n    (contains? d ::dht) (assoc :dht (::dht d))\n    (::indexer d) (assoc :indexer (::indexer d))))\n\n\n(defn- link-context\n  \"What a `yin.link` call is answered under (yin.repl.query/serve): the\n   reader's authority, the publisher's key, and the requesting VM's\n   primitives and module registry -- the modules it linked are derived\n   from it, never recorded -- and the round.\"\n  [state vm]\n  {:authority (link/authority (:link-source state))\n   :key (:dht-key state)\n   :primitives (:primitives vm)\n   :modules (:modules vm)\n   :round (:round state)})\n\n\n(defn- admission-context\n  \"The context the session's admission interpreter answers under\n   (`yin.repl.admission/context`): its own key's principal and the\n   shell token.\"\n  [state]\n  (admission/context {:key (:dht-key state) :session (:shell-token state)}))\n\n\n(defn- serve-admission\n  \"One round of the session's in-process admission interpreter, or nil\n   when the session runs none.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-let [interp (:admitter state)]\n    (admission/serve {:interpreter interp\n                      :policy (get-in state [:link-source :admission])\n                      :context (admission-context state)}\n                     link/serve-budget)))\n\n\n(defn- drive-links\n  \"Serve the linker interpreter and run the parked VM alternately, at most\n   `link-round-budget` rounds, while `vm` waits on a link.  A round that\n   moves nothing ends the drive: a link whose content source cannot\n   answer will not answer by waiting longer.  Returns\n   `[state vm pending progress?]`, `pending` the links the interpreter\n   reported `:pending`, and `progress?` true when a round moved\n   something -- advanced a serve cursor, delivered a response or\n   completed an install -- the fact the pending run's `:checks` resets\n   on (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3.1).  A refused or lost link\n   raises as the VM's own, carrying the interrupted VM's minted\n   identity.\n\n   The admission interpreter serves right after the linker interpreter\n   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5): a question appended and a question\n   answered are each progress, so a require asked about and answered in\n   process completes within the drive, two rounds later.\n\n   A VM waiting on a `dao.space.query/q` call is driven the same way: the\n   query interpreter (`yin.repl.query/serve`) answers from the session's\n   indexer and the VM runs on.  Only a round the VM spends waiting on a\n   link counts against `link-round-budget`; a query is answered in the\n   round it is asked, so its rounds are bounded by `query-drive-budget`\n   calls instead: a VM still waiting on a call once the drive has\n   answered that many raises `query-call-limit-text` as its own error,\n   the unanswered request abandoned with it.\"\n  [state vm]\n  (loop [i 0\n         calls 0\n         vm vm\n         state state\n         pending []\n         progress? false]\n    (let [link? (link-waiting? vm)\n          query? (query/waiting? vm)]\n      (cond\n        (or (vm/halted? vm) (not (or link? query?)) (>= i link-round-budget))\n        [state vm pending progress?]\n\n        (and query? (>= calls query-drive-budget))\n        (throw (link-raise (ex-info query-call-limit-text\n                                    {:reason :yin.repl.query/call-limit\n                                     :limit query-drive-budget})\n                           vm\n                           (update state :query-pair query/abandon-requests)))\n\n        :else\n        (let [served (when link?\n                       (link/serve {:pair (:link-pair state)\n                                    :source (:link-source state)\n                                    :dht (:dht state)\n                                    :admission (:admission state)}))\n              state (cond-> state\n                      served (assoc :link-pair (:pair served)\n                                    :dht (:dht served)\n                                    :admission (:admission served)))\n              admitted (when link? (serve-admission state))\n              state (cond-> state\n                      admitted (assoc :admitter (:interpreter admitted)))\n              answered (when query?\n                         (query/serve {:pair (:query-pair state)\n                                       :indexer (:indexer state)\n                                       :ast-indexer (:ast-indexer state)\n                                       :dht (:dht state)\n                                       :link (link-context state vm)\n                                       :limits {:row-limit query-row-limit\n                                                :byte-limit query-byte-limit}\n                                       :budget (min query-serve-budget\n                                                    (- query-drive-budget\n                                                       calls))}))\n              state (cond-> state\n                      answered (assoc :query-pair (:pair answered)\n                                      :dht (:dht answered)\n                                      :indexer (:indexer answered)))\n              pending (if (seq (:pending served)) (:pending served) pending)]\n          (if (or (:progress? served)\n                  (:progress? admitted)\n                  (:progress? answered))\n            (let [vm' (try (vm/run vm)\n                           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error)\n                                  error\n                             (throw (link-raise error vm state))))]\n              (recur (if link? (inc i) i)\n                     (+ calls (:answered answered 0))\n                     vm'\n                     state\n                     pending\n                     true))\n            [state vm pending progress?]))))))\n\n\n(defn- tokenize\n  \"Answer the halted VM's value on the output medium under `state`'s\n   round, as the evaluator runner does for a program it runs itself.  A\n   resumed require halts outside the observer loop, so the shell emits\n   its token here.\"\n  [state vm]\n  ((make-runner (:output-stream state) (round-id state)) vm))\n\n\n(defn- pending-text\n  [pending]\n  (if (seq pending)\n    (str \";; require pending: \"\n         (str/join \", \" (map (fn [p]\n                               (str (pr-str (:name p))\n                                    \" (link \" (pr-str (:yin.link/id p))\n                                    (when (:admission p)\n                                      \", awaiting admission\")\n                                    \")\"))\n                             pending))\n         \"); lines typed meanwhile run when it completes, (abandon) gives\"\n         \" up\\n\")\n    (str \";; require still pending; lines typed meanwhile run when it\"\n         \" completes, (abandon) gives up\\n\")))\n\n\n(defn- dropped-lines-text\n  [n]\n  (when (pos? n)\n    (str \";; dropped \" n \" line\" (when (> n 1) \"s\")\n         \" typed while the require was pending\\n\")))\n\n                                               (:trimmed in)\n                                               (:parsed in))]\n              (recur state' (str text \"\\n\" text') more)))))\n\n\n(defn- recheck-pending*\n  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run`: serve the\n   interpreter, run the parked VM, and either answer its value -- the\n   round the require began in finally completes, and the lines retained\n   while it was pending, then `input`, evaluate against it -- consult\n   the link policy when the re-check leaves the run pending, `:checks`\n   counting this pending run's re-checks that made no progress and\n   resetting on one that did, or, when the re-check raised the link's\n   refusal, return the shell to the round's base with the error as text\n   and evaluate `input` there.  `input` is nil for the host's\n   `recheck-pending`, which evaluates no line of its own.\"\n  [state input]\n  (let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n    (try\n      (let [[state' vm' pending progress?] (drive-links state (:vm parked))]\n        (if (vm/halted? vm')\n          (let [vm'' (engine/restore-initial-env (:env (:base parked)) vm')\n                [st text] (finalize-eval state\n                                         (cond-> (assoc state' :vm vm'')\n                                           (:frontend parked)\n                                           (assoc ::frontend\n                                                  (:frontend parked)))\n                                         (tokenize state' vm''))]\n            (fold-queued [(assoc st :vm vm'' :pending-run nil) text]\n                         (cond-> (vec (:pending-lines parked))\n                           input (conj input))))\n          (let [checks (if progress? 0 (inc (or (:checks parked) 0)))\n                parked' (cond-> (assoc parked\n                                       :vm vm'\n                                       :links pending\n                                       :checks checks)\n                          input (update :pending-lines\n                                        (fnil conj []) input))\n                [st text] (drain-output (assoc state'\n                                               :vm vm'\n                                               :pending-run parked'))]\n            (consult-link-policy st text (pending-text pending)))))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n        (let [[st text] (drain-output state)\n              d (ex-data error)]\n          (fold-queued\n            [(carry-served (assoc st\n                                  :vm (query/discard-answers\n                                        (carry-link-identity\n                                          (:base parked)\n                                          {:id-counter (::link-counter d)\n                                           :origins (::link-origins d)})\n                                        (:query-pair st))\n                                  :pending-run nil)\n                           d)\n             (str text\n                  (format-error error)\n                  (dropped-lines-text (count (:pending-lines parked))))]\n            (cond-> [] input (conj input))))))))\n\n\n(defn recheck-pending\n  \"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\n   the step an unattended host drives at its own cadence\n   (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 4): serve the interpreter, run the\n   parked VM, and consult the link policy when the run is still\n   pending.  A re-check that completes the run folds the retained lines\n   exactly as a typed line's completion does.  Returns `[state text]`,\n   `text` nil when nothing is pending.  It reads no clock and takes no\n   callback; the host decides when to call it.\"\n  [state]\n  (if (:pending-run state)\n    (recheck-pending* state nil)\n    [state nil]))\n\n\n(defn recheck-on-load-events\n  \"The host ticker's re-check of a pending run over a DHT link source\n   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2): `recheck-pending`, once, if and only if\n   `events` -- one tick's `dao.space.dht/step` events and head follower\n   events -- hold a `:loaded` or `:load-failed` event for a manifest a\n   pending link waits on, or an `:installed` head of a principal a\n   pending link awaits (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.6, first contact).\n   Any other event, and any event while nothing waits on it, answers\n   `[state nil]` with `state` itself: no re-check, no `:checks`.\"\n  [state events]\n  (let [links (get-in state [:pending-run :links])\n        waits (set (keep :manifest links))\n        heads (set (mapcat :principals links))]\n    (if (some (fn [e]\n                (or (and (contains? #{:loaded :load-failed}\n                                    (:dao.space.dht/event e))\n                         (contains? waits (:manifest e)))\n                    (and (= :installed (:yin.head/event e))\n                         (contains? heads (:principal e)))))\n              events)\n      (recheck-pending state)\n      [state nil])))\n\n\n(defn recheck-on-answers\n  \"The host ticker's re-check of a pending run parked on an admission\n   question (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5 and 8.2), beside\n   `recheck-on-load-events`: serve the in-process admission interpreter\n   when the session runs one, drain at most `serve-budget` answers off\n   the answer medium, and keep the successor state whatever matched --\n   irrelevant answers are consumed and gone.  `recheck-pending` runs\n   once if and only if a retained answer's admission id is the\n   `:admission` of a pending link; otherwise the answer is `[state'\n   nil]`, with no re-check and no `:checks`.  With nothing pending it\n   still drains.  No clock: the host decides when to call it.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-let [adm (:admission state)]\n    (let [admitted (serve-admission state)\n          state (cond-> state\n                  admitted (assoc :admitter (:interpreter admitted)))\n          adm (admission/drain adm link/serve-budget)\n          state (assoc state :admission adm)\n          waiting (set (keep :admission\n                             (get-in state [:pending-run :links])))]\n      (if (some #(contains? waiting %) (keys (:answers adm)))\n        (recheck-pending state)\n        [state nil]))\n    [state nil]))\n\n\n(defn- resume-pending\n  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` behind a typed\n   line: while the run stays pending the line is retained -- the parked\n   VM owns the store a new evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates,\n   in typing order and exactly once, when the link completes.\"\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (recheck-pending* state {:trimmed trimmed, :parsed parsed}))\n\n\n(defn- command-line?\n   the root's custody: the mode only. An ungated root leaves it as is.\"\n  [child mode]\n  (cond-> child\n    (some? mode) (assoc :yin.k/gate mode)))\n\n\n(defn- spawn-child\n  \"`loading` (section 7.3): a fresh child of the parent's backend over the\n   verified image, under a fresh origin tag, its install ancestry the\n   parent's plus this module, and a module view of its own: each linked\n   entry the parent holds is attached and lowered into the child's\n   coordinates here, never the parent's lowered values reused. The\n   child's capability secret comes from the composition's\n   `:secret-source`, a function of the child's origin tag; a composition\n   that supplies none gives the child no secret, so the child can issue\n   no resource reference (fail closed).\"\n  [state module-name response]\n  (let [n (or (:origins state) 0)\n        origin (keyword (str (name (or (:origin state) :t0)) \".\" n))\n        registry (reduce (fn [r [m entry]]\n                           (module/assoc-module r m (dissoc entry :bindings)))\n                         (:modules state)\n                         (linked-entries (:modules state)))\n        source (:secret-source state)\n        child (module/spawn-module state\n                                   (:value (:image response))\n                                   {:modules registry,\n                                    :origin origin,\n                                    :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry state))\n                                                    module-name),\n                                    ;; the composition mints each task's\n                                    ;; secret (r10); without a source the\n                                    ;; child can issue no reference\n                                    :capability-secret\n                                    (when (fn? source) (source origin))})\n        child (reduce (fn [c [m entry]] (receive-module c m entry))\n                      child\n                      (linked-entries registry))]\n    [(stamp-gate child (vm/gate-mode state)) (assoc state :origins (inc n))]))\n\n\n(defn- wake-installed\n  \"Move every `:install` wait entry naming `module-name` to the ready\n   queue, woken with `value`, or with `refusal` raised.\"\n  [state module-name value refusal]\n  (let [waiter? (fn [e]\n                  (and (= :install (:reason e)) (= module-name (:name e))))\n        waiters (filter waiter? (:wait-set state))]\n    (-> state\n        (update :wait-set (fn [ws] (filterv (complement waiter?) ws)))\n        (update :ready-queue (fnil into [])\n                (map (fn [e]\n                       (if refusal (refused-entry e refusal) (ready e value))))\n                waiters))))\n\n\n(defn- refuse-install\n  \"`refused` (section 7.3): nothing from the child's store is published,\n   every waiter is restored with the refusal as the effect's error, and\n   the install entry is removed so a later require may try again.\"\n  [state module-name refusal]\n  (-> state\n      (update :installs dissoc module-name)\n      (wake-installed module-name nil refusal)))\n\n\n(defn- verified-images\n  \"Every image this scheduler verified that the child's slice may name as\n   an origin: the install's own, and those held by identity under the\n   registry of the child or of the receiving task (section 7.3, act 2).\"\n  [state child response]\n  (into [(:value (:image response))]\n        (mapcat (fn [[_ entry]] (vals (:images entry))))\n        (concat (linked-entries (:modules child))\n                (linked-entries (:modules state)))))\n\n\n(defn- link-install\n  \"`validated` then `linked` (section 7.3): the child reached halt; every\n   export must be a key of its store (`:export-missing`); the slice is\n   lifted (act 1) and its origins checked against the images this\n   scheduler verified (act 2, `:foreign-image`); the receiving task then\n   receives, first, the entry -- its store snapshots win over the plain\n   registry snapshot of a dependency, since the child's mutations are\n   what the slice carries -- and then every module the child linked that\n   it lacks (acts 3 and 4), and every waiter is restored with the name.\n   A response that rode on an admission allow records it on the entry\n   under `:admission`.\"\n  [state module-name {:keys [vm response]}]\n  (let [manifest (:manifest response)\n        address (manifest-address response)\n        exports (sort-by str (:yin.module/exports manifest))\n        missing (vec (remove #(contains? (:store vm) %) exports))]\n    (if (seq missing)\n      (refuse-install state module-name\n                      {:status :refused,\n                       :reason :export-missing,\n                       :module module-name,\n                       :names missing})\n      (let [lifted (try (lift-slice vm address exports)\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                          {:refusal (error-refusal module-name e)}))]\n        (if-let [refusal (:refusal lifted)]\n          (refuse-install state module-name refusal)\n          (let [verified (verified-images state vm response)\n                origin-of (fn [seg]\n                            (some #(when (module/image-holds? vm % seg) %)\n                                  verified))\n                foreign (first (remove origin-of\n                                       (sort-by str (:origins lifted))))]\n            (if (some? foreign)\n              (refuse-install state module-name\n                              {:status :refused,\n                               :reason :foreign-image,\n                               :module module-name,\n                               :segment foreign})\n              (let [images (into {}\n                                 (map (fn [seg]\n                                        (let [img (origin-of seg)]\n                                          [(module/image-identity vm img)\n                                           img])))\n                                 (:origins lifted))\n                    entry (module/module-entry\n                            (:modules (module/link-module\n                                        nil manifest (:derivation response)\n                                        (assoc lifted :images images)))\n                            module-name)\n                    ;; the admission the link rode on (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n                    ;; 7.5): inherited and transferred with the entry\n                    entry (cond-> entry\n                            (= :allow (:yin.admit/decision response))\n                            (assoc :admission\n                                   (select-keys response\n                                                [:yin.admit/id\n                                                 :yin.admit/decision\n                                                 :yin.admit/asserters\n                                                 :yin.admit/address])))\n                    received (receive-module state module-name entry)\n                    received (reduce\n                               (fn [s [m dep]]\n                                 (if (some? (module/module-entry\n                                              (:modules (:modules s)) m))\n                                   s\n                                   (receive-module s m (dissoc dep :bindings))))\n                               received\n                               (linked-entries (:modules vm)))]\n                (-> received\n                    (update :installs dissoc module-name)\n                    (wake-installed module-name module-name nil))))))))))\n\n\n(defn- advance-install\n  \"Step the install child of `module-name` in this round, beside every\n   other task (section 7.3): `running` runs it until it halts or parks.\n   A parked child stays `parked`; a halted one goes on to `validated`; an\n   error refuses the install. An error while publishing -- attaching an\n   `ok` the entry waits in `:link-response`; on `full` it stays in\n   `:link-request` and the poll retries it. Under a custody gate the mint\n   and the append are the driver's: the entry is built without `:cursor`\n   and parks in `:link-request` with nothing sent. The entry is the kernel's\n   registers plus the link fields: resource ids and plain data, never a\n   handle.\n\n   A module already on this task's install ancestry is `:require-cycle`\n   naming the chain (section 7.4): the child that asked is refused. A VM\n   composed without a link pair cannot link, so its miss fails as v1's\n   did, naming the modules it has.\"\n  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns]}]\n  (let [module-name (:module effect)\n        build (get park-entry-fns :module/require)\n        registers #(if build (build state effect nil) {})\n        resources (:resources state)\n        response (get resources link-response-resource)]\n    (cond\n      (some? (resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\n      {:value module-name, :state state, :blocked? false}\n\n      (some #{module-name} (:ancestry state))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Require cycle\"\n                      {:reason :require-cycle,\n                       :module module-name,\n                       :chain (conj (vec (:ancestry state)) module-name)}))\n\n      (installing? state module-name)\n      (block-on state (assoc (registers) :reason :install :name module-name))\n\n      (not (and response (get resources link-request-resource)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\\[yin\\\\.repl\\\\.(link|admission)(\\\\s|\\\\])' src test --glob '\"'!cljd-out/**'\"'; sed -n '65,270p' src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc; sed -n '385,435p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '514,660p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '2065,2140p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc; rg -n 'principal-admission|:admit|quote.*require|require.*quote' src/cljc/yang/python src/cljc/yin/vm/publication.cljc; nl -ba collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\\[yin\\\\.repl\\\\.(link|admission)(\\\\s|\\\\])' src test --glob '\"'!cljd-out/**'\"'; sed -n '65,270p' src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc; sed -n '385,435p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '514,660p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '2065,2140p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc; rg -n 'principal-admission|:admit|quote.*require|require.*quote' src/cljc/yang/python src/cljc/yin/vm/publication.cljc; nl -ba collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:20:    [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:23:    [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:46:    [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:47:    [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:12:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:22:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yin/repl/require_test.cljc:28:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_doc_test.cljc:11:            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_doc_test.cljc:12:            [yin.repl.link :as link]))\ntest/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:31:    [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:25:            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:27:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\ntest/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:34:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:19:            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:23:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:63:            [yin.repl.link :as link]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:40:            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn make-state\n  \"The composition's admission state over a fresh pair of `capacity`\n   elements each: the question and answer media, the answer cursor\n   minted at the answer medium's oldest end before any answer exists,\n   nothing asked, nothing answered, serial 0.  An unread answer is\n   evicted when the unread backlog exceeds `capacity`: the host bounds\n   that backlog by its production rate and drain cadence, and an\n   evicted answer's question stays open until its request is retired.\"\n  [capacity]\n  (let [questions (medium capacity)\n        answers (medium capacity)]\n    {:pair {:questions questions\n            :answers answers\n            :cursor (oldest answers)}\n     :asked {}\n     :answers {}\n     :serial 0}))\n\n\n(defn- answer-link-id\n  \"The link id component of answer `a`'s admission id, or nil when the\n   answer carries no `[link-id serial]`.\"\n  [a]\n  (let [id (when (map? a) (:yin.admit/id a))]\n    (when (and (vector? id) (= 2 (count id)))\n      (first id))))\n\n\n(defn- keep-answer\n  \"`admission` with answer `a` retained when its id is exactly the id of\n   the question asked for its link id and no answer is held for it yet:\n   the first answer wins, and a duplicate, a stale serial, or an answer\n   for an unknown or retired id correlates to nothing and is dropped.\"\n  [admission a]\n  (let [id (:yin.admit/id a)\n        asked (get-in admission [:asked (answer-link-id a)])]\n    (if (and (some? asked)\n             (= id (:yin.admit/id asked))\n             (not (contains? (:answers admission) id)))\n      (assoc-in admission [:answers id] a)\n      admission)))\n\n\n(defn drain\n  \"Consume at most `budget` elements of the answer medium from the\n   composition's persisted cursor, keeping the answers that match a\n   question still asked (`keep-answer`), and answer the successor state\n   with the cursor past everything read.  A gap adopts the recovery\n   cursor the transport answers -- the earliest retained position,\n   never an evicted one -- and continues within the budget; blocked or\n   end stops.  The same function serves a link round and the host's\n   recheck hook.\"\n  [admission budget]\n  (let [answers (get-in admission [:pair :answers])]\n    (loop [admission admission\n           left budget]\n      (if (<= left 0)\n        admission\n        (let [r (stream/next answers (get-in admission [:pair :cursor]))\n              admission' (assoc-in admission [:pair :cursor]\n                                   (:dao.stream/cursor r))]\n          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n            :dao.stream/ok (recur (keep-answer admission'\n                                               (:dao.stream/value r))\n                                  (dec left))\n            :dao.stream/gap (recur admission' (dec left))\n            admission))))))\n\n\n(defn ask\n  \"Append the question for link `request` over the resolved `entry` of\n   its name, bound to that resolution: the manifest address, every\n   asserter, and the entry's provenance verbatim, with the request's own\n   format and contract.  Answers `{:admission a :id id}` with the\n   question retained under its link id and the serial advanced, or\n   `{:admission admission}` unchanged when the medium refused it.\"\n  [admission request entry]\n  (let [link-id (:yin.link/id request)\n        id [link-id (:serial admission)]\n        provenance (:yin.link/provenance entry)\n        question {:yin.admit/id id\n                  :yin.link/id link-id\n                  :yin.admit/name (:yin.link/name request)\n                  :yin.admit/address (:address entry)\n                  :yin.admit/asserters (vec (:yin.module/asserted-by\n                                              provenance))\n                  :yin.admit/provenance provenance\n                  :yin.link/format (:yin.link/format request)\n                  :yin.link/contract (:yin.link/contract request)}]\n    (if (ok? (stream/append! (get-in admission [:pair :questions]) question))\n      {:admission (-> admission\n                      (assoc-in [:asked link-id] question)\n                      (update :serial inc))\n       :id id}\n      {:admission admission})))\n\n\n(defn asked\n  \"The question `admission` holds for `link-id`, or nil.\"\n  [admission link-id]\n  (get-in admission [:asked link-id]))\n\n\n(defn answer-to\n  \"The retained answer to `question`, or nil.\"\n  [admission question]\n  (get-in admission [:answers (:yin.admit/id question)]))\n\n\n(def ^:private allow-keys\n  #{:yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/conditions})\n\n\n(defn judge\n  \"nil when `answer` allows with empty conditions; otherwise the refusal\n   it amounts to, as `{:yin.admit/reason r ...}`.  A refusal keeps the\n   answer's reason and open keys.  An allow's key set is closed: exactly\n   id, decision and conditions.  Non-empty conditions refuse\n   `:yin.admit/unsupported-condition` and anything else that is not such\n   an allow or a refusal with a keyword reason refuses\n   `:yin.admit/malformed-answer`: both fail closed.\"\n  [answer]\n  (let [decision (:yin.admit/decision answer)\n        conditions (:yin.admit/conditions answer)\n        allow? (and (= :allow decision)\n                    (= allow-keys (set (keys answer)))\n                    (map? conditions))]\n    (cond\n      (and allow? (empty? conditions)) nil\n\n      allow?\n      {:yin.admit/reason :yin.admit/unsupported-condition\n       :yin.admit/conditions conditions}\n\n      (and (= :refuse decision) (keyword? (:yin.admit/reason answer)))\n      (dissoc answer :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision)\n\n      :else {:yin.admit/reason :yin.admit/malformed-answer})))\n\n\n(defn settle\n  \"`admission` with the question for `link-id` and its answer dropped:\n   the link's response has landed.\"\n  [admission link-id]\n  (let [q (asked admission link-id)]\n    (cond-> admission\n      q (-> (update :asked dissoc link-id)\n            (update :answers dissoc (:yin.admit/id q))))))\n\n\n(defn forget\n  \"`admission` with every question and answer of the retired link ids\n   `link-ids` dropped.  A later answer for one correlates to nothing and\n   `drain` drops it.\"\n  [admission link-ids]\n  (let [gone (set link-ids)]\n    (-> admission\n        (update :asked #(reduce dissoc % gone))\n        (update :answers\n                #(into {} (remove (fn [[id _]] (contains? gone (first id)))) %)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The interpreter's half\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn context\n  \"The composition-owned context `verify` receives, from the session:\n   the subject, the principal of the composition's own key (nil without\n   one), and the session token.  Authorization vocabulary stays here and\n   in the policy; the question and the linker carry none.\"\n  [{:keys [key session]}]\n  {:yin.admit/subject (when key (sign/principal (:public key)))\n   :yin.admit/session session})\n\n\n(defn trusted-asserter\n  \"The default verify: allow when some asserter of `question` is in the\n   `decision` set, else refuse `:yin.admit/untrusted-principal` naming\n   the asserters.\"\n  [decision _context question]\n  (let [asserters (vec (:yin.admit/asserters question))]\n    (when-not (some #(contains? decision %) asserters)\n      {:yin.admit/reason :yin.admit/untrusted-principal\n       :yin.admit/asserters asserters})))\n\n\n(defn- composed\n  \"One verify of `verify`: a function, or a sequence of them composed so\n   the first reason wins.\"\n  [verify]\n  (cond\n    (nil? verify) trusted-asserter\n    (fn? verify) verify\n    :else (fn [decision context question]\n            (some #(% decision context question) verify))))\n\n\n(defn policy\n  \"The interpreter's policy from a composition's `:admission` option:\n   `:own` the composition's own principals, `:trusted` an explicit set\n   of principal ids (`ed25519:<hex>`), `:verify` a verify function or a\n   sequence of them, and the decision snapshot: a static `:decision`, or\n   the newest value of a capacity-1 `:decision-medium`, or by default\n\n(defn- admission-refusal\n  \"The link refusal an admission refusal `r` (`admission/judge`'s\n   shape) of question `q` amounts to: the answer's reason and open keys\n   in the link refusal shape.\"\n  [q r]\n  (merge (dissoc r :yin.admit/reason)\n         {:status :refused\n          :reason (:yin.admit/reason r)\n          :name (:yin.admit/name q)\n          :yin.admit/id (:yin.admit/id q)\n          :yin.admit/decision :refuse}))\n\n\n(defn- admitted\n  \"A request whose admission question was asked (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n   7.5): pending while unanswered, with no re-resolution; refused as the\n   answer says; or, allowed, attempted against the address the question\n   was bound to, never a fresh resolution.  An `:ok` response names the\n   admission it rode on.\"\n  [node declared request q a]\n  (cond\n    (nil? a) {:node node, :body ::pending, :asking (:yin.admit/id q)}\n\n    (some? (admission/judge a))\n    {:node node, :body (admission-refusal q (admission/judge a))}\n\n    :else\n    (let [{:keys [node body waits]}\n          (dht-attempt node declared request (:yin.admit/address q))]\n      {:node node\n       :waits waits\n       :asking (when (= ::pending body) (:yin.admit/id q))\n       :body (if (= :ok (:status body))\n               (assoc body\n                      :yin.admit/id (:yin.admit/id q)\n                      :yin.admit/decision :allow\n                      :yin.admit/asserters (:yin.admit/asserters q)\n                      :yin.admit/address (:yin.admit/address q))\n               body)})))\n\n\n(defn- dht-answer\n  \"The DHT branch of `answer`: a request already asked about goes by\n   its question (`admitted`); otherwise its name is resolved.  A direct\n   `:name-env` entry, provenance `:composition`, is the composition's\n   own and is not asked; a signed name passes the language runtime's\n   `:admit`, when there is one, and is then asked: the question is\n   appended and the link parks on it.  With no admission state the\n   question cannot be asked, `:yin.admit/unconfigured`.\"\n  [source node admission request]\n(defn serve\n  \"One serve round of the interpreter over the link pair: read every\n   request `pair`'s cursor has not yet consumed and answer each in\n   request order, at most `budget` of them.  The first request nothing\n   can answer yet stops the round -- the requests behind it keep their\n   order -- and is reported under `:pending`; its cursor stays, so a\n   later round re-reads and re-attempts it.  A response the response\n   medium refuses reports its request pending the same way, and the\n   round reports no progress.  A content source links each manifest under\n   the composition's `:derivation` policy (`composition`'s option,\n   `:verifying` unless the composition asked for `:trusted`), and an\n   `:ok` response of a lowered format names its `:trust`.  `dht` is the\n   shell's DHT node, which a DHT source reads and advances.  Returns\n   `{:pair pair :pending pending :progress? bool :dht node :admission a}`,\n   `:progress?` true when at least one response or admission question\n   was appended, so the shell knows the round moved something; a\n   pending entry a DHT load holds names that load's manifest under\n   `:manifest`, one awaiting a first head names those principals under\n   `:principals`, and one parked on an admission question names its id\n   under `:admission`.\n\n   `admission` is the composition's admission state\n   (`yin.repl.admission/make-state`, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5): the\n   round first drains the answer medium (`admission/drain`, at most\n   `budget` elements), and the successor state is answered under\n   `:admission`, with the question and answer of every request whose\n   response landed dropped.\"\n  ([comp] (serve comp serve-budget))\n  ([{:keys [pair source dht admission]} budget]\n   (loop [pair pair\n          node dht\n          admission (some-> admission (admission/drain budget))\n          remaining budget\n          pending []\n          progress? false]\n     (let [done {:pair pair, :pending pending, :progress? progress?,\n                 :dht node, :admission admission}]\n       (if (zero? remaining)\n         done\n         (let [r (stream/next (:requests pair) (:cursor pair))]\n           (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n             ;; blocked, or a gap: nothing more is answerable this round\n             done\n             (let [request (:dao.stream/value r)\n                   link-id (:yin.link/id request)\n                   res (answer source node admission request)\n                   {:keys [node body waits heads asking asked?]} res\n                   admission (get res :admission admission)\n                   answered? (and (not= ::pending body)\n                                  (respond! pair request body))]\n               (if answered?\n                 (recur (assoc pair :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n                        node\n                        (some-> admission (admission/settle link-id))\n                        (dec remaining)\n                        pending\n                        true)\n                 {:pair pair\n                  :pending (conj pending\n                                 (cond-> {:name (:yin.link/name request)\n                                          :yin.link/id link-id}\n                                   waits (assoc :manifest waits)\n                                   heads (assoc :principals heads)\n                                   asking (assoc :admission asking)))\n                  :progress? (or progress? (true? asked?))\n                  :dht node\n                  :admission admission})))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Retirement of an abandoned run (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn run-descriptor\n  \"The run an abandon retires: link ids `[origin k]` with `from <= k <\n   until` of `:ids`, and every install child origin `origin.m` with\n   `from <= m < until` of `:children`, with its descendants.  `base` is\n   the VM the run began from, `parked` the VM it was given up as; an\n   absent counter is zero.  Both counters mint the current value then\n   increment, so each interval is half-open.\"\n  [base parked]\n  {:origin (or (:origin parked) :t0)\n   :ids [(or (:id-counter base) 0) (or (:id-counter parked) 0)]\n   :children [(or (:origins base) 0) (or (:origins parked) 0)]})\n\n\n(defn- run-owned?\n  \"Whether link id `id` belongs to `run`: its own origin within `:ids`,\n   or an install child origin within `:children` exactly, or one of its\n   descendants -- matched on the child's name followed by \\\".\\\", never\n   a raw prefix, so `:t0.10` is not a descendant of `:t0.1`.\"\n  [id {:keys [origin ids children]}]\n  (when (and (vector? id) (= 2 (count id)) (keyword? (first id))\n             (integer? (second id)))\n    (let [[o k] id\n          [from until] ids\n          [cfrom cuntil] children\n          on (name o)]\n      (or (and (= o origin) (<= from k) (< k until))\n          (some (fn [m]\n                  (let [child (str (name origin) \".\" m)]\n                    (or (= on child)\n                        (str/starts-with? on (str child \".\")))))\n                (range cfrom cuntil))))))\n\n\n(defn retire\n  \"Retire the requests of an abandoned `run` (`run-descriptor`) still\n   unread on `pair`: walking from the request cursor, each request the\n   run owns is passed over with no response -- the engine has already\n   retired its id, so a response would be late -- and the first request\n   it does not own stops the walk, keeping request order.  Every\n   admission question and answer of a retired request is dropped.\n   Returns `{:pair p :admission a :retired [link-id ...]}`.\"\n  [{:keys [pair admission]} run]\n  (loop [pair pair\n         retired []]\n    (let [r (stream/next (:requests pair) (:cursor pair))\n          id (:yin.link/id (:dao.stream/value r))]\n      (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n               (run-owned? id run))\n        (recur (assoc pair :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) (conj retired id))\n        {:pair pair\n         :admission (some-> admission (admission/forget retired))\n         :retired retired}))))\n      :responses responses})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Publishing (the mint-side counterpart the tests and compositions use)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn publish!\n  \"Store `image` in `handle` and return its index datom\n   `[identity attribute address]`. The address is the store's own\n   `segment-key`; the identity is the format's own mint. The caller owns\n   the index: nothing is recorded here. The two storage-derived formats\n   mint through `yin.vm/materialize-tree!` and\n   `yin.vm.code/materialize-vector!` instead (section 9).\"\n  [handle format image]\n  (let [address (jing/materialize! handle image)]\n    [((:identity-fn format) image) (address-attribute format) address]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Manifest-delivered images (section 8.1)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- declared-obligation\n  \"The manifest's declaration of a retained free name, as the obligation\n   record that travels with the image (section 4.2 step 5a): a name\n   under `:yin.module/primitives` becomes a primitive obligation\n   carrying the profile address; a name under `:yin.module/requires` --\n   the required module itself, or a name qualified by it -- becomes a\n   module obligation carrying the required manifest's address. Nil when\n   the manifest declares the name nowhere.\"\n  [manifest obligation]\n  (let [sym (obligation-name obligation)\n        primitives (:yin.module/primitives manifest)\n        requires (:yin.module/requires manifest)\n        module (or (when (and (symbol? sym) (namespace sym))\n                     (let [m (symbol (namespace sym))]\n                       (when (contains? requires m) m)))\n                   (when (contains? requires sym) sym))]\n    (cond\n      (contains? primitives sym)\n      {:name sym, :kind :primitive, :profile (get primitives sym)}\n      (some? module)\n      {:name sym, :kind :module, :module module,\n       :manifest (get requires module)}\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn- manifest-join\n  \"Step 5a's manifest half (section 4.2): every retained occurrence is\n   joined with the manifest that delivered the image and becomes its\n   declaration's own obligation record. A name the manifest declares\n   nowhere is `:undeclared-free`: the publisher did not say what the\n   name means, so no receiver can bind it identically.\"\n  [manifest obligations]\n  (or (some (fn [obligation]\n              (when-not (declared-obligation manifest obligation)\n                (refused :undeclared-free\n                         {:name (obligation-name obligation)})))\n            obligations)\n      (mapv (fn [obligation]\n              (declared-obligation manifest obligation))\n            obligations)))\n\n\n(defn- with-identity-indexes\n  \"Seed the linker-local indexes of the storage-derived formats a\n   manifest link reads -- the manifest, the record, the tree, the\n   vector -- with the identity function (section 3): each one's identity\n   is its own address. A composition's own entries are left alone.\"\n  [state]\n  (reduce (fn [state format-kw]\n            (update-in state [:indexes format-kw]\n                       (fn [index] (or index identity))))\n          state\n          [(:format manifest-format) (:format record-format)\nrg: src/cljc/yin/vm/publication.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/safepoint.cljc:202:      [(u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote prelude/module-name)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/safepoint.cljc:203:       (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote module-name)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1972:  (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote m))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc:19:   reaching `py`'s state. `principal-admission` is the explicit refusal\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc:130:(defn principal-admission\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc:132:   (`yin.repl.link/composition`'s `:admit`), until L-e: a name resolved\n     1\tPlan file saved. Here is the complete revised design.\n     2\t\n     3\tCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-12 14:21 GMT\n     4\tCompleted-Local: 2026-10-12 21:21 +07 (Asia/Bangkok)\n     5\t\n     6\t**Verdict.** The relocation stands; the importer idea is withdrawn. Codex's four P1s were all correct and are fixed below. The content driver is dropped from the evidence, the exposure rule follows the registry and its installation family, the tick now hands its round's successor and progress to the pending driver, and AL-1 becomes a pure relocation with the API reduction in AL-2. The owner's correction supersedes section 3: there is no language at the linker level.\n     7\t\n     8\t## 0. Owner correction, applied\n     9\t\n    10\tAll languages compile to the universal AST. yin.vm does not know the source language and the linker must not either. No linker datum carries a language, a frontend or an `[id revision]`: `:yin.link/importer` and `:yin.admit/importer` are deleted from this design, the closed request key set is not edited, and no kernel constructor or `spawn-module` changes. Admission is about principals (signing keys that asserted a name), addresses (A, the only code identity) and names. \"Who is asking\" is the holder: a composition-owned context the interpreter receives as the `context` argument of `(verify decision context question)`, today built by `admission/context` from the session's own key. A published module is AST at an address; any frontend may import it when the holder's policy admits that principal for that address. Registry reuse between frontends is not a linker security question. Frontend runtime-state isolation (ruling 18, Python's `py.rt` cells) is a frontend and session concern outside the linker and is not designed here.\n    11\t\n    12\t## 1. Layering\n    13\t\n    14\tRule: linker semantics is what a plain Clojure consumer (dht.md section 10) must have to resolve, ask, bind, deliver, discharge or retire a link. REPL is what disappears with the REPL: cadence, display, retained lines, which principals this session names.\n    15\t\n    16\tEvidence, verified: `test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:46-47` requires both REPL namespaces to run a Python DHT import; `test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:34` and `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:12` require `yin.repl.link` to mint a pair and serve a VM-level request. The request-serving semantics (resolve, ask, bind, deliver, retire) exists only in `yin.repl.link/serve`. Correction: `dao.jing.content.driver` requires only dao.jing, dao.jing.content.step and dao.stream (`src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj:20`); its docstring names yin.repl.link as a downstream consumer. It is not evidence and is not re-required; its docstring is updated in AL-1.\n    17\t\n    18\t| Lives in | Contents |\n    19\t|---|---|\n    20\t| `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` (from `yin.repl.link`) | pair minting, `composition`, `authority`, `serve`, `run-descriptor`, `retire`, `formats`, constants; after AL-2 also `make`, `round`, `reconfigure` |\n    21\t| `yin.vm.linker.admission` (from `yin.repl.admission`) | protocol unchanged: `make-state`, `drain`, `ask`, `asked`, `answer-to`, `judge`, `settle`, `forget`, `context`, `trusted-asserter`, `policy`, `interpreter`, `serve`, `reasons` |\n    22\t| `yin.vm.engine` / `yin.vm.module` | the `:admission` registry record as landed; the pinned-dependency check (section 5) |\n    23\t| `yin.repl` | configuration (`:link-source`, `:admission` option, `--dht-trust`, `:external`), one `:linker` value after AL-2, one tick hook, trust commands, display text |\n    24\t\n    25\tNeither new namespace requires any `yin.repl*` namespace; follow, authority and configuration stay supplied data. Old namespaces deleted, no shim.\n    26\t\n    27\t## 2. The linker's admission boundary\n    28\t\n    29\tDatums: question and answer shapes of 7.5.1 verbatim, no added key. Allow key set closed at id, decision, conditions; a refusal keeps reason and open keys.\n    30\t\n    31\tMinting (AL-2): `interpreter/make` mints the link pair and, only for a `:dht?` source, the admission pair and answer cursor. A local or remote content source has no admission pair.\n    32\t\n    33\tWhere the wait lives: a parked link is a request the interpreter's request cursor has not passed plus a retained question under `:asked` (`link.cljc:399` and `:427`). Nothing lands on the response medium until the answer does, so the VM's wait entry never learns admission exists. No new state.\n    34\t\n    35\tOne round, `(interpreter/round linker node budget)`, in order: drain answers (one bounded drain per round, the `admission/drain` semantics), serve link requests stopping at the first pending, serve the in-process interpreter when the value holds one. Returns the successor value, the node, the pending entries and a progress flag. Progress is any of: a response appended, a question appended, an in-process answer appended, a drained answer matched a retained question. The successor is always carried, even without progress.\n    36\t\n    37\tAttachment: in process, `:admission` builds the policy (`trusted-asserter` over own plus `:trusted`, or a composed `:verify` over a static `:decision` or a capacity-1 `:decision-medium`). External, `:admission :external` mints the pair and runs no interpreter; another process reads questions and appends answers over any dao.stream exposure, no privileged node. ShiBi attaches as either with no linker edit.\n    38\t\n    39\tAuthority versus admission: declared principals (R8) decide which assertions count in the fold; trusted principals decide which resolved entries the holder accepts. Independent inputs. A `:composition` provenance entry is never asked.\n    40\t\n    41\tDischarge and L-d: ask after resolve, before load; discharge is step 5b after delivery, untouched. An admission refusal is a section 9 link refusal, so try-require catches it as it catches `:absent`. An install child's transitive requirement is asked on its own request.\n    42\t\n    43\t**Exposure, stated exactly.** Admission governs entry into a registry. An allow admits one address into the requesting task's registry, and authorization follows that registry and its installation-family inheritance: `link-install` spawns the child over the parent's linked entries and receives each into it (`engine.cljc` ~1289-1307); the child's installs transfer back to the parent with the `:admission` record (~1396-1403); a name already resolvable in the registry answers with no link request and hence no question (`module.cljc` ~552-554). The exposure domain is the installation family for its life, not one task. It is about principal plus address plus holder context, and it is language-blind: any frontend compiling to a require of that name hits the same entry. \"Untrust is not retroactive\" means `(untrust p)` changes the decision snapshot for questions not yet answered; it evicts no registry entry, revokes no appended response, and leaves a question already answered allow allowed. `(reset)` and `(vm ...)` start a fresh registry and fresh admission state.\n    44\t\n    45\t## 3. The tick-to-VM handoff\n    46\t\n    47\tChosen: the tick retains the round's successor and passes its progress into the pending driver, which runs the VM once before requiring another round to report progress. One hook replaces `recheck-on-load-events` and `recheck-on-answers`: `(recheck-on-tick state events)`.\n    48\t\n    49\t1. Run one `round` on the session's `:linker` with the session node; assoc the successor and node into state before anything else, so a raising VM run carries it (`link-raise` keeps the one `::linker` key, `carry-served` restores it).\n    50\t2. If the round reported progress, call the pending driver with progress carried in. `drive-links` gains an initial-progress argument: its first iteration runs the VM once without a round of its own (no second drain before that run), then continues the existing loop, bounded by `link-round-budget`.\n    51\t3. Else, if the events hold a loaded or load-failed event for a manifest a pending link waits on, or an installed head of an awaited principal, recheck as today. The no-progress `:checks` counter and the link policy are unchanged.\n    52\t4. Else nothing happens.\n    53\t\n    54\tAcceptance (AL-2, three hosts): (a) a require parks on an external question and the initial drive stops; an allow is appended; one tick's round delivers the response and the run completes with no further question, input line, load event or answer. (b) The same with an empty decision medium at park time and a snapshot appended after parking: the in-process interpreter answers in one tick's round, the drain matches and the response lands inside the driver's loop, and the run completes. (c) A refusal arriving the same way raises as the VM's own with the successor `:linker` carried into the rolled-back state. (d) A tick with no progress and no relevant event rechecks nothing and leaves `:checks` unchanged.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 4. What to do with what landed\n    57\t\n    58\t| AD-1 piece | Ruling |\n    59\t|---|---|\n    60\t| `yin.repl.admission` | MOVE to `yin.vm.linker.admission` (AL-1); `context` keeps `:yin.admit/session` through AL-1, AL-3 replaces it |\n    61\t| `yin.repl.link` | MOVE to `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` (AL-1), API preserved |\n    62\t| admission pair in `make-session` | untouched in AL-1; AL-2 moves it into `make`, dht-only |\n    63\t| `serve-admission`, `admission-context`, `:admitter`, `recheck-on-answers` | untouched in AL-1; AL-2 deletes them |\n    64\t| `link-raise` / `carry-served` | AL-2: carry one `::linker` key |\n    65\t| `abandon-pending` | AL-2: one `retire` call |\n    66\t| `--dht-trust`, `:admission`, `:external` | KEEP, configuration |\n    67\t| engine `:admission` registry record | KEEP |\n    68\t| `admission_test`, `admission_doc_test` | MOVE to test/yin/vm/linker/ (AL-1) |\n    69\t\n    70\tAD-2 (delete Python `principal-admission` and the `:admit` hook; `publication.cljc:130` still present) is compatible and lands first; AL-1 rebases over it. AD-3 becomes AL-4.\n    71\t\n    72\t## 5. Trust versus safety; the pinned-dependency fix\n    73\t\n    74\tUnchanged: trust is the interpreter's answer, safety is the linker's and L-e's, an allow never relaxes L-e, conditions stay empty.\n    75\t\n    76\tQ4, wording corrected: `declared-obligation` (`linker.cljc` ~2088) recognizes a retained free name equal to the required module or qualified by it. Python's imported dependency arrives through a quoted require and module-object operations, not such a retained name, so no module obligation exists and discharge compares nothing; the DHT source's dependency-bindings check is the only guard. Fix, engine seat, lands with L-d, independent of admission: in the `linked` transition before lifting or publishing the installed slice, check every pinned require of the manifest against the halted child's linked entry for that name; absent or unequal refuses `:dependency-pin-mismatch`. Acceptance bypasses the DHT early guard and covers inherited and freshly installed mismatches on all four VMs. AL-0 corrects the false 7.4 sentence.\n    77\t\n    78\t## 6. Slices, inventory, gates\n    79\t\n    80\tConsumer inventory (require forms, verified by grep, excluding test/cljd-out): `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:19,23`; `src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:40`; `src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:63`; `test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:46-47`; `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:20`; `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:23`; `test/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:25,27`; `test/yin/repl/admission_doc_test.cljc:11-12`; `test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:22`; `test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:31`; `test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc:28`; `test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:34`; `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:12`. Docstring mentions (publication.cljc:132, driver.clj:7, repl.cljc, store_write_audit_test.clj:368, linker_require_test.cljc:1323) are text edits.\n    81\t\n    82\tGate ladder (docs/agents/build-n-test.md): G0 iterate `bb test:sub:clj <own>`; G1 checkpoint `bb test:sub yin.vm yin.repl yang.python`, adding `dao.jing` when a dao.jing file is edited (AL-1's driver docstring is one); G2 land `bb test:changed` on three lanes plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` where slow tests exist; G3 master `bb test` after merge; G4 slow tier at phase boundaries, after AL-2 and after AL-4. Before any Dart lane after a rename, `rm -rf test/cljd-out` so the aggregator does not pick up stale generated files.\n    83\t\n    84\t- **AL-0 docs.** dht.md 7.5 rewritten as the linker's admission with section 0's ruling, 7.5.7 replaced by section 2's exposure text, 7.4 corrected; linker.md new 6.5 and section 10 updated; dao.shibi.md first-consumer paragraph names the linker; yang.antlr.md ~3044 pointer; docs/agents/architecture.md gains the layering rule; src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md pointer. Acceptance: `admission-doc-test` green on three hosts against the rewritten section.\n    85\t- **AL-1 relocation** (linker seat). `git mv` both namespaces and both admission tests; every public var and the session topology preserved (`composition` and `serve` keep their names; `:link-pair`, `:admission`, `:admitter`, `serve-admission`, `recheck-on-answers` untouched); all require forms updated; store-write allowlist key moved to `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc` with the same `composition` entry; driver docstring updated. Acceptance: admission tests, `require_test`, `dht_test`, `linker_require_test`, `derive_test` green on three hosts; the namespace-dependency check is empty:\n    86\t\n    87\t```\n    88\tgrep -rn -E '^\\s*\\[yin\\.repl(\\.[a-z-]+)? ' src/cljc/yin/vm src/cljc/yang src/clj/dao --include='*.clj*'\n    89\t```\n    90\t\n    91\t  It matches require vectors only, so docs and datum vocabulary such as `:yin.repl/root` and error keywords do not match. `bb test:sub:list yin.vm` shows the two new test namespaces; slow `dht_import_test` green on the JVM. Collab note to the yang.python orchestrator before touching its tests.\n    92\t- **AL-2 REPL reduction and handoff** (REPL seat, with the linker-side `make` and `round` in the same slice). Acceptance: section 3 (a) to (d); F3, P1-2 (i) and (iii), P2-3 against `round`; lexical: `repl.cljc` requires `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` and not `yin.vm.linker.admission`; no session keys `:admission` or `:admitter`; no calls to `drain`, `judge`, `ask`, `settle` or the admission `serve`; exactly one tick hook; configuration plumbing and display text allowed.\n    93\t- **AL-3 holder context** (linker seat). `composition` gains an optional `:holder` (a principal id, or a token the verify understands); `context` answers the subject from it, defaulting to the own key's principal; `:yin.admit/session` deleted; `reconfigure` replaces the policy of a `:linker` value while preserving the interpreter's cursors, retained questions, serials and external mode. Acceptance, three hosts: a recording verify receives the subject the composition supplied; reconfiguring to a new trusted set answers a still-parked question under the new decision with cursors and serials unchanged.\n    94\t- **AL-4 trust commands** (REPL seat). `(trust p)`, `(untrust p)`, `(trusted)` edit the `:trusted` configuration and call `reconfigure`. Acceptance: AD-3's list through `round`, plus untrust-not-retroactive from section 2.\n    95\t\n    96\tOrder: AD-2, AL-0, AL-1, AL-2, AL-3, AL-4. Slow tier after AL-2 and AL-4.\n    97\t\n    98\tMust not land before L-e: any claim an untrusted-origin import is safe; a default decision beyond own principals; honoring a non-empty condition; weakening profile, pin or export-origin checks; admission in a frontend or on the content pair. The design is AST-level data on streams; the register-VM cutover does not touch it.\n    99\t\n   100\t**Unverified.** AD-2 lane results (source still has the hook). That `bb test:sub` maps the relocated tests into `yin.vm` by prefix (subsystems.edn suggests yes). That `yin.repl.dht-process-test` needs no edit beyond requires. The Python no-retained-name claim comes from codex and I1, not a run. Nothing was run or edited; the plan file at `/Users/sto/.claude/plans/created-gmt-2026-10-12-14-00-00-gmt-curried-wreath.md` holds this same text.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The revised design addresses the registry exposure and late-allow handoff issues in the current source. The require inventory also matches my search. I’m checking the documentation-test acceptance and remaining slice boundaries before deciding the verdict."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yin/repl/admission_doc_test.cljc; sed -n '120,170p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc; sed -n '1950,2025p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '120,195p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '265,380p' src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc; rg -n 'yin\\\\.repl|:admit|admission|timeout' src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj; cat subsystems.edn; sed -n '115,175p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; sed -n '1480,1515p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yin/repl/admission_doc_test.cljc; sed -n '120,170p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc; sed -n '1950,2025p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '120,195p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '265,380p' src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc; rg -n 'yin\\\\.repl|:admit|admission|timeout' src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj; cat subsystems.edn; sed -n '115,175p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; sed -n '1480,1515p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.admission-doc-test\n  \"The executable check of slice AD-0 (yin.vm.linker.dht.md section 7.5,\n   \\\"Pinned by test\\\"): the section and the code must not diverge.  It\n   reads the section and asserts that every reason the admission seam\n   refuses with is named in it, that it names `serve-budget` and\n   `pair-capacity` with the values the vars hold, and that its retire\n   rule spells the delimited prefix `origin + \\\".\\\"`.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]])\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\n            [yin.repl.link :as link]))\n\n\n(def ^:private spec-path\n  \"docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\")\n\n\n(defn- read-text!\n  [path]\n  #?(:cljd (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n             (when (.existsSync f) (.readAsStringSync f)))\n     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. ^String path)]\n            (when (.exists f) (slurp f)))\n     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")]\n             (when (.existsSync fs path)\n               (.readFileSync fs path \"utf8\")))))\n\n\n(defn section-7-5\n  \"The text of section 7.5 of `text`, its subsections included, from its\n   heading to the next heading of level three or higher, or nil.\"\n  [text]\n  (let [lines (str/split-lines (or text \"\"))\n        heading? #(re-find #\"^#{1,3} \" %)\n        start (first (keep-indexed (fn [i l]\n                                     (when (re-find #\"^### 7\\.5 \" l) i))\n                                   lines))]\n    (when start\n      (str/join \"\\n\" (cons (nth lines start)\n                           (take-while (complement heading?)\n                                       (drop (inc start) lines)))))))\n\n\n(defn- value-named\n  \"The digits the section gives in parentheses after the code name\n   `word`, as in `serve-budget` (64), or nil.\"\n  [section word]\n  (second (re-find (re-pattern (str word \"`? \\\\(([0-9]+)\\\\)\")) section)))\n\n\n(defn divergences\n  \"Every way section 7.5 of `text` and the code diverge, as data: empty\n   when they agree.\"\n  [text]\n  (let [section (section-7-5 text)]\n    (if (nil? section)\n      [{:missing :section-7.5}]\n      (cond-> (vec (keep (fn [r]\n                           (when-not (str/includes? section (str r))\n                             {:missing r}))\n                         (sort-by str admission/reasons)))\n        (not= (str link/serve-budget) (value-named section \"serve-budget\"))\n        (conj {:serve-budget (value-named section \"serve-budget\")\n               :code link/serve-budget})\n\n        (not= (str link/pair-capacity) (value-named section \"pair-capacity\"))\n        (conj {:pair-capacity (value-named section \"pair-capacity\")\n               :code link/pair-capacity})\n\n        (not (str/includes? section \"origin + \\\".\\\"\"))\n        (conj {:missing \"origin + \\\".\\\"\"})))))\n\n\n(deftest admission-spec-test\n  (testing (str \"section 7.5 of \" spec-path \" and the code agree\")\n    (is (= [] (divergences (read-text! spec-path))))))\n                                           :package? package?,\n                                           :py-address py-address,\n                                           :deps deps}))]\n             (if (= :refused (:status res))\n               (reduced (assoc res :unit n))\n               (assoc-in acc [:addresses n] (:address res)))))\n         {:status :ok, :addresses {}}\n         (:order plan))))))\n\n\n(defn principal-admission\n  \"The admission a Python link source applies to each name it resolves\n   (`yin.repl.link/composition`'s `:admit`), until L-e: a name resolved\n   from signed assertions is admitted when one of the importer's own\n   principals, the public keys `publics` (64 lowercase hex), asserts it\n   -- it vouches for that very manifest address -- and a direct entry,\n   the composition's own, always. Any other is refused\n   `:yang.python.antlr/foreign-principal` with the `:name`, its\n   `:asserters`, and `:requires` `:L-e`, before anything of it links.\"\n  [publics]\n  (let [own (set (map sign/principal publics))]\n    (fn [name entry]\n      (let [provenance (:yin.link/provenance entry)\n            asserters (:yin.module/asserted-by provenance)]\n        (when-not (or (= :composition provenance) (some own asserters))\n          (refused :yang.python.antlr/foreign-principal\n                   {:name name,\n                    :asserters (vec asserters),\n                    :requires :L-e}))))))\n                           (lower-module-body packet)))]\n     (u/mark-tails\n       (case prelude\n         :bundled (if-not (preseeded-imports-only? pk)\n                    (throw (ex-info\n                             \"Imports need the linked prelude (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6)\"\n                             {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unsupported,\n                              :construct \"import under the bundled prelude\"}))\n                    (u/then prelude/uast main))\n         :linked (u/seq-nodes\n                   (into [(app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))]\n                         (concat (mapv #(app* 'require (u/lit %)) requires)\n                                 [(app* 'py/init!) main]))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: one Python unit as the linker module pym.<name>\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- require-node\n  \"(require 'm) as a tree node.\"\n  [m]\n  (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote m))))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The exports of a compiled Python unit: its spec and body, immutable\n   after install (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6's module shape).\"\n  '#{spec body})\n\n\n(defn module-packet\n  \"One ok packet as the linker module `pym.<mangled>`: one wide\n   application whose operands are `(require 'py)`, one `(require\n   'pym.<i>)` per statically imported module (delivery hoisted and\n   pinned, bodies lazy), then the spec and body definitions. `name` is\n   the dotted Python module name and `package?` (default false) whether\n   the unit is a package, which is source layout, not derivable from\n   rows: the spec records both, the runtime derives `__package__` from\n   them, and the lowering resolves relative imports against them. The\n   body is the same form `lower-packet` runs as `__main__`: one code\n   image, two roles.\"\n  [packet {:keys [name package?]}]\n  (when (or (empty? name)\n            (str/starts-with? name \".\")\n            (str/ends-with? name \".\")\n            (str/includes? name \"..\")\n            (str/includes? name \"$\"))\n    (throw (ex-info \"a module name is dotted identifiers\"\n                    {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unsupported,\n                     :construct \"malformed module name\",\n                     :name name})))\n  (let [unit {:name name, :package? (boolean package?)}\n        requires (import-requires (p/validate! packet) unit)\n        nodes (into [prelude/module-name] requires)\n        defs [(u/def! 'spec (u/lit unit))\n              (u/def! 'body (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym]\n                                   (lower-module-body packet unit)))]\n        operands (into (mapv require-node nodes) defs)\n        params (mapv (fn [i] (symbol (str \"%d\" i))) (range (count operands)))]\n    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) operands))))\n\n\n(defn- declare-free-name\n  \"The `:primitives` entry free name `n` declares over `registry`, or nil\n   when `covered` (the requirement-pinned module names) covers it.\"\n  [registry covered n]\n  (if (and (symbol? n) (some? (namespace n))\n           (contains? covered (symbol (namespace n))))\n    nil\n    (if-let [profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives n)]\n      [n profile]\n      (if-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n        (let [entry (module/module-entry (:modules registry)\n                                         (symbol (namespace n)))\n              f (get-in entry [:slice (symbol (name n))])]\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"The content side of the shell's link composition, from the host's\n   creation options.  `content-store` is a `dao.jing` byte-store handle\n   served in process over its own ring-buffer content pair (the\n   single-process and durable-local rows of section 6.1);\n   `content-client` is the linker's content-pair client map\n   `{:requests w :answers r :cursor c}` on a connection whose far end\n   serves content (the remote-content row), and the drive then only\n   steps the linker, the server running elsewhere (section 6.4).  A\n   content source is optional: with none, every link stays `:pending`\n   and says so.  Supplying both is a composition defect.  `dht?` is the\n   DHT link source (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1): it reads content from the\n   node each serve round is handed, holds nothing here, and is refused\n   together with either content source.\n\n   `principals` are the public keys (64 lowercase hex) whose signed name\n   assertions the reader honors (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.1), and `key`\n   the node's own publisher key, whose principal is declared too (6.5):\n   a node resolves the names it published.  Only the public half is\n   kept here.  `follow` are the principal ids (`ed25519:<hex>`) whose\n   published heads the DHT source follows (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md\n   5.6): a name that is `:absent` while one of them has no installed head\n   is pending on it, not refused.\n\n   `derivation` is the composition's derivation policy (section 8.1) for\n   the manifest links it serves from a content source: `:verifying`, the\n   default, or `:trusted`, which only a composition that is its own\n   publisher asks for. The response names the trust it applied.\n\n   `admit`, optional, is a language runtime's admission of each name the\n   DHT source resolves, `(admit name entry)` with the `names` entry: nil\n   admits, a refusal body refuses the request before any load or link\n   (a Python source's foreign-principal refusal, yang.antlr.md 8.5.6\n   ruling 19).\n\n   `admission`, optional, is the policy of the in-process admission\n   interpreter (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5, `yin.repl.admission/policy`):\n   `{:trusted #{principal} :verify f :decision d :decision-medium m}`,\n   the key's own principal joining it as `:own`.  Without it no\n   interpreter runs in process: the questions a DHT source asks are\n   answered elsewhere or not at all.\"\n  [{:keys [name-env content-store content-client dht? principals key\n           follow derivation admit admission]}]\n  (when (and content-store content-client)\n    (throw (ex-info \"content-store and content-client are exclusive\"\n                    {:content-store content-store})))\n  (when (and dht? (or content-store content-client))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"a dht:<dir> index store is the link source; \"\n                         \"content-store and content-client are refused with it\")\n                    {:dht? dht?})))\n  {:name-env (or name-env {})\n   :principals (vec (distinct (cond-> (vec principals)\n                                key (conj (:public key)))))\n   :follow (vec follow)\n   :derivation (or derivation :verifying)\n   :admit admit\n   :admission (when admission\n                (admission/policy\n                  (assoc admission\n                         :own (when key #{(sign/principal (:public key))}))))\n   :content (cond\n              dht? {:kind :dht}\n\n              content-store\n              {:kind :local\n               :store content-store\n               :requests (medium content-capacity)\n               :responses (medium content-capacity)}\n\n              content-client\n              {:kind :remote, :client content-client}\n\n              :else nil)})\n\n(defn policy\n  \"The interpreter's policy from a composition's `:admission` option:\n   `:own` the composition's own principals, `:trusted` an explicit set\n   of principal ids (`ed25519:<hex>`), `:verify` a verify function or a\n   sequence of them, and the decision snapshot: a static `:decision`, or\n   the newest value of a capacity-1 `:decision-medium`, or by default\n   the union of own and trusted principals.\"\n  [{:keys [own trusted verify decision decision-medium] :as opts}]\n  (let [principals (into (set own) trusted)]\n    (cond-> {:own (set own)\n             :trusted (set trusted)\n             :verify (composed verify)}\n      decision-medium (assoc :decision-medium decision-medium)\n      (contains? opts :decision) (assoc :decision decision)\n      (not (or decision-medium (contains? opts :decision)))\n      (assoc :decision principals))))\n\n\n(defn interpreter\n  \"The in-process interpreter's state over `admission`'s pair under\n   `policy`: the two media, its question cursor minted at the oldest\n   end, and its decision-medium cursor when the policy names one.\"\n  [admission policy]\n  (let [{:keys [questions answers]} (:pair admission)\n        decisions (:decision-medium policy)]\n    (cond-> {:questions questions\n             :answers answers\n             :cursor (oldest questions)}\n      decisions (assoc :decision-cursor (oldest decisions)))))\n\n\n(defn- read-decisions\n  \"`interp` after reading the decision medium to its present end: the\n   newest value read is the snapshot, an ended medium is `:ended?`.\"\n  [interp medium]\n  (loop [interp interp]\n    (let [r (stream/next medium (:decision-cursor interp))]\n      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n        :dao.stream/ok (recur (assoc interp\n                                     :decision-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n                                     :snapshot (:dao.stream/value r)\n                                     :snapshot? true))\n        :dao.stream/gap (recur (assoc interp\n                                      :decision-cursor\n                                      (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n        :dao.stream/end (assoc interp :ended? true)\n        interp))))\n\n\n(defn- snapshot\n  \"`interp` with this round's decision snapshot, read once.\"\n  [interp policy]\n  (if-let [medium (:decision-medium policy)]\n    (read-decisions interp medium)\n    (assoc interp :snapshot (:decision policy) :snapshot? true)))\n\n\n(defn- decide\n  [interp policy context question]\n  (let [base {:yin.admit/id (:yin.admit/id question)}]\n    (if (:ended? interp)\n      (assoc base\n             :yin.admit/decision :refuse\n             :yin.admit/reason :yin.admit/decision-ended)\n      (let [r ((:verify policy) (:snapshot interp) context question)]\n        (cond\n          (nil? r) (assoc base\n                          :yin.admit/decision :allow\n                          :yin.admit/conditions {})\n          (map? r) (merge r base {:yin.admit/decision :refuse})\n          :else (assoc base :yin.admit/decision :refuse))))))\n\n\n(defn serve\n  \"One round of the interpreter: read the decision snapshot once, then\n   answer at most `budget` questions in order, one answer each.  With no\n   snapshot yet and the decision medium not ended, nothing is answered\n   and the questions stay.  `verify` runs synchronously on the one\n   snapshot; it opens, fetches and waits for nothing.  An answer the\n   medium refuses stops the round with its question unread.  Returns\n   `{:interpreter i :progress? bool :answered n}`.\"\n  [{:keys [interpreter policy context]} budget]\n  (let [interp (snapshot interpreter policy)]\n    (if-not (or (:ended? interp) (:snapshot? interp))\n      {:interpreter interp, :progress? false, :answered 0}\n      (loop [interp interp\n             n 0\n             left budget]\n        (let [done {:interpreter interp, :progress? (pos? n), :answered n}]\n          (if (<= left 0)\n            done\n            (let [r (stream/next (:questions interp) (:cursor interp))]\n              (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n                :dao.stream/ok\n                (let [a (decide interp policy context (:dao.stream/value r))]\n                  (if (ok? (stream/append! (:answers interp) a))\n                    (recur (assoc interp :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n                           (inc n)\n                           (dec left))\n                    done))\n\n                :dao.stream/gap\n                (recur (assoc interp :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n                       n\n                       (dec left))\n\n                done))))))))\ntest/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj:368:   ;; a VM store; the same shape as yin.repl.link's composition\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:1:(ns yin.repl.frontends\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:5:   names a language's namespace; `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:19:    [yin.repl :as repl]))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:84:  \"`yin.repl/create-state` composed with the standard catalog unless the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:1:(ns yin.repl.link\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:5:   The shell composes the link pair per VM (`yin.repl/make-session`) and\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:40:            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:151:   `admit`, optional, is a language runtime's admission of each name the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:157:   `admission`, optional, is the policy of the in-process admission\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:158:   interpreter (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5, `yin.repl.admission/policy`):\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:164:           follow derivation admit admission]}]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:177:   :admit admit\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:178:   :admission (when admission\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:179:                (admission/policy\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:180:                  (assoc admission\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:386:(defn- admission-refusal\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:387:  \"The link refusal an admission refusal `r` (`admission/judge`'s\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:400:  \"A request whose admission question was asked (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:404:   admission it rode on.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:409:    (some? (admission/judge a))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:410:    {:node node, :body (admission-refusal q (admission/judge a))}\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:432:   `:admit`, when there is one, and is then asked: the question is\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:433:   appended and the link parks on it.  With no admission state the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:435:  [source node admission request]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:438:        q (some-> admission (admission/asked (:yin.link/id request)))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:440:      (admitted node declared request q (admission/answer-to admission q))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:443:                      (when-some [admit (:admit source)] (admit name entry)))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:457:          (nil? admission)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:464:          (let [{:keys [id] :as asked} (admission/ask admission request entry)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:467:             :admission (:admission asked)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:478:   yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.6), or an admission question not yet\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:480:   it, the successor admission state under `:admission`).  `:node` is\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:484:  [source node admission request]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:493:              :defect :yin.repl/name-required}}\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:495:      dht? (dht-answer source node admission request)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:527:   `{:pair pair :pending pending :progress? bool :dht node :admission a}`,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:528:   `:progress?` true when at least one response or admission question\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:532:   `:principals`, and one parked on an admission question names its id\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:533:   under `:admission`.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:535:   `admission` is the composition's admission state\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:536:   (`yin.repl.admission/make-state`, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5): the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:537:   round first drains the answer medium (`admission/drain`, at most\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:539:   `:admission`, with the question and answer of every request whose\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:542:  ([{:keys [pair source dht admission]} budget]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:545:          admission (some-> admission (admission/drain budget))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:550:                 :dht node, :admission admission}]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:559:                   res (answer source node admission request)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:561:                   admission (get res :admission admission)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:567:                        (some-> admission (admission/settle link-id))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:577:                                   asking (assoc :admission asking)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:580:                  :admission admission})))))))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:626:   admission question and answer of a retired request is dropped.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:627:   Returns `{:pair p :admission a :retired [link-id ...]}`.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:628:  [{:keys [pair admission]} run]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:637:         :admission (some-> admission (admission/forget retired))\ncat: subsystems.edn: No such file or directory\n- **Layer 2 (Execution Engine)**: `yin.vm.ucf`, `yin.vm`\n- **Layer 3 (Languages & Interop)**: `yin.repl`, `yang.python`, `yang.base`\n- **Layer 4 (Applications & Demos)**: `demo`, `world`\n- **Infrastructure**: `dev`, `bench`\n\nPrerequisites (`build:yin-repl-peer`, `build:yin-repl-node`, `gen:python-antlr`)\nand lane serialization (`[:clj :cljd]`) are derived purely from text reach of the\nselected namespaces and run automatically when needed.\n\n#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n\n1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n4. **G3 Master**: The mandatory landing gate on master after merge, and for any wide change (`bb test`).\n5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`), and at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track (owner decision 2026-10-12; see \"Test tiers: quick and slow\" below). G0 to G3 run the quick tier; G4 runs the slow tier.\n\n\nThe linker-over-DHT end-to-end gate (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md,\nslice L5) is two tests:\n\n- `yin.repl.dht-process-test` (JVM lane only): real `yin.repl.main`\n  processes over real loopback UDP. A JVM publisher with a key file\n  publishes modules by name, and JVM and Node readers require them by\n  name on all four VMs. Plain Clojure in the test JVM takes the same path\n  and checks each section 9 failure as data. Ports are ephemeral, and\n  every wait is bounded. A run takes a few minutes. Run it alone with\n  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n  `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\n- `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (all three lanes): the same\n  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\n  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\n  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n  REPL.\n\n```sh\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\nThe Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\nnamespaces that use `dao.test-slow/guard` and fails if one has no generated\nDart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\nwith its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n`--config-merge` for `test:slow:cljs`); it is not a ready-to-use regex, and it\nexits 1 when no namespace uses the guard. `flutter test` spends about 7.5 s loading\neach of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\nscript compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n(greedy by file size; each imports its files and calls their `main`), runs\n`flutter test --concurrency N` on the shards, and deletes them. Shards never sit\nunder `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\n   :order [],\n   :routes {},\n   :outbox [],\n   :next-fetch 0})\n\n\n(def ^:private request-keys\n  \"The closed key set of a link request (section 6.3).\"\n  #{:yin.link/id :yin.link/format :yin.link/contract :yin.link/name\n    :yin.link/identity :yin.link/scan?})\n\n\n(defn- portable-scalar?\n  \"Whether `x` is a value a link request may carry beside its id: a\n   scalar, keyword, symbol, or address -- never a function, handle,\n   collection, or host object (section 6.3).\"\n  [x]\n  (or (nil? x) (true? x) (false? x) (number? x) (string? x)\n      (keyword? x) (symbol? x)))\n\n\n(defn- link-id?\n  \"Whether `x` is a well-formed link id: the `[origin counter]` pair of\n   section 7.2, two non-nil portable scalars.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (vector? x)\n       (= 2 (count x))\n       (every? (fn [e] (and (some? e) (portable-scalar? e))) x)))\n\n\n(defn- in-flight?\n  \"Whether `id` names a link whose completion is still owed.\"\n  [state id]\n  (or (contains? (:links state) id)\n      (some (fn [c] (= id (:yin.link/id c))) (:outbox state))))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\s*\\\\[yin\\\\.repl(\\\\.[a-z-]+)? ' src/cljc/yin/vm src/cljc/yang src/clj/dao --glob '*.clj*'; rg --files | rg 'subsystems.edn|admission-in-linker-r2.prompt|AD-2|ad-2'; sed -n '325,340p' test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj; sed -n '1,46p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '730,815p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; rg -n 'recheck-on-(answers|load-events)' src test --glob '\"'!**/cljd-out/**'\"'; cat collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\s*\\\\[yin\\\\.repl(\\\\.[a-z-]+)? ' src/cljc/yin/vm src/cljc/yang src/clj/dao --glob '*.clj*'; rg --files | rg 'subsystems.edn|admission-in-linker-r2.prompt|AD-2|ad-2'; sed -n '325,340p' test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj; sed -n '1,46p' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc; sed -n '730,815p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; rg -n 'recheck-on-(answers|load-events)' src test --glob '\"'!**/cljd-out/**'\"'; cat collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"src/dev/subsystems.edn\ncollab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md\ncollab/1792263000000-reviewer-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md\n   ;; the expander consumer's macro store\n   \"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"\n   {[\"inject-last-value\" \"update\"] 1\n    [\"make-expander\" :map] 1}\n   ;; the content source descriptor: `:store` names a dao.jing byte-store\n   ;; handle the linker interpreter serves content from, never a VM store\n   \"src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc\"\n   {[\"composition\" :map] 1}\n   ;; the handoff demo: shipped definitions, checked\n   \"src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc\"\n   {[\"datoms->semantic-vm\" \"update\"] 1}\n   ;; a JVM demo moving one VM's whole store to another\n   \"src/clj/yin/demo.clj\"\n   {[\"run-demo\" \"assoc\"] 1}\n   ;; the handoff lower's isolated-store install (UCF 7.6.2): every\n   ;; carried key goes through store-put -- a reserved key inside a\n(ns yin.repl.link\n  \"The REPL's linker-side composition (yin.vm.linker.md sections 6.1 and 9,\n   M5): the interpreter box of the four-stream topology.\n\n   The shell composes the link pair per VM (`yin.repl/make-session`) and\n   the content pair per content source; this namespace owns the second\n   and answers what the first receives.  One serve round reads every link\n   request the interpreter has not yet seen, resolves each by name\n   through the composition's name environment -- the snapshot the host\n   supplies, an authority fold (`yin.vm.linker.authority/name-environment`)\n   reduced to `name -> manifest address` -- and links the manifest's\n   image over the content pair, appending the response the requesting\n   task correlates on (section 7.2, steps 5 to 6).\n\n   Step 5b is deferred: the obligations travel on the response and the\n   receiving task's engine discharges them against its live state\n   (section 7.2, step 7), so the interpreter passes\n   `:defer-discharge` to `link-manifest` and discharges nothing here.\n\n   Liveness is the composition's (section 6.3, D6): an attempt serves the\n   content pair for at most `attempt-budget` drive rounds and then\n   reports the link `:pending` -- nothing is appended, the request is\n   re-read and re-attempted on a later round, and `abandon` is the\n   shell's.  No clock, no atom, no global: every input is an argument or\n   a composition value, and every outcome is plain data.\n\n   A DHT link source (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1) holds no\n   handle: each serve round receives the shell's `dao.space.dht` node\n   and answers the node after it.  A resolved name whose closure is not\n   loaded starts its load (`yin.vm.linker.dht/load-module`) and reports\n   the link `:pending`, naming the manifest it waits on; the node's own\n   step fetches.  A failed load is refused in its section 9 shape and\n   forgotten; a loaded one has its dependency bindings checked, then\n   links over a local runtime on the node's store, asking no peer.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.jing.content :as content]\n            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\n            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as linker.dht]\n            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n\n\n(def pair-capacity\n    program-out))\n\n\n(defn- make-session\n  \"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\n   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\n   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\n   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\n   lifetime.\n\n   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\n   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\n   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\n   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\n   (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\n   round advances each, and neither calls the other.  It records\n   `shell-token` as provenance and publishes into `index-store`.  The AST\n   indexer (`yin.repl.ast-index`), holding the session's `$ast` and `$occ`\n   relations, is a third such peer.\n\n   The link pair is the session's (`yin.repl.link/make-pair`): the VM's\n   half lives in its private `:resources`, the interpreter's half beside\n   it under `:link-pair`.  The content pair and the name environment the\n   interpreter serves from are the shell's (`:link-source`), and outlive\n   a session rebuild.\n\n   The admission state is the session's too (`yin.repl.admission`,\n   yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5): the question and answer media beside the\n   link pair under `:admission`, and, when the shell's link source names\n   an admission `policy`, the in-process interpreter's own state over\n   them under `:admitter`.\n\n   The query call pair is the session's too (`yin.repl.query/make-pair`):\n   the VM's half is its FFI pair, the interpreter's half with its request\n   cursor sits under `:query-pair`, and the interpreter answers from the\n   session's `:indexer`, and `:ast-indexer` for `$ast` and `$occ`, as they\n   stand when it serves.\n\n   A durable store's HEAD write travels with the store handle\n   (`:head-fn`, yin.repl.store): every session the store outlives\n   publishes through the same one.\"\n  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives shell-token index-store policy]\n  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n        admission (admission/make-state link/pair-capacity)\n        query-pair (query/make-pair query-pair-capacity)\n        vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives pair query-pair)\n        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\n        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n    {:vm vm\n     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\n     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\n     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n     :observer (:observer program-in)\n     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n     :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n                                   :session-token shell-token\n                                   :content-store index-store\n                                   :after-publish (:head-fn index-store)})\n     :ast-indexer (ast-index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))})\n     :link-pair pair\n     :admission admission\n     :admitter (when policy (admission/interpreter admission policy))\n     :query-pair (dissoc query-pair :out-cursor)}))\n\n\n(defn- checked-link-policy\n  \"Validate the `:link-policy` creation option, failing closed at\n   assembly (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3): `:manual` is the\n   default and today's behavior, a function `(fn [view])` is the\n   embedder's rule, and `:lease` is reserved for the phase-2 deadline --\n   refused, not implemented yet.  Anything else is refused with the\n   supported values named.\"\n  [policy]\n  (cond\n    (or (nil? policy) (= :manual policy)) :manual\n    (fn? policy) policy\n    :else\n    (throw\n      (ex-info\n        (if (= :lease policy)\n          \"Yin REPL :link-policy :lease is not implemented yet\"\n          \"Unknown Yin REPL :link-policy\")\n        {:link-policy policy\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2016:(defn recheck-on-load-events\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2040:(defn recheck-on-answers\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2043:   `recheck-on-load-events`: serve the in-process admission interpreter\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:1005:   (yin.repl/recheck-on-load-events), a completed hydration installed, a\ntest/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:120:                             [s text] (repl/recheck-on-load-events s events)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:1034:   of its own (yin.repl/recheck-on-load-events, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2),\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:1036:   drained (yin.repl/recheck-on-answers, 7.5): its text prints after the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:1050:      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-load-events (:repl state) events)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:1051:            [repl answered] (shell/recheck-on-answers repl)\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1054:                  [repl' text'] (repl/recheck-on-load-events repl [late late])\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1056:                  [waiting' text''] (repl/recheck-on-load-events waiting\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:1931:                            [s text] (repl/recheck-on-load-events s events)]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:689:                       (first (settle (first (repl/recheck-on-answers\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:792:          [state text] (repl/recheck-on-answers (answer-at! state (allow id2)))]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:800:        (let [[state' text] (repl/recheck-on-answers\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:814:                   [(first (repl/recheck-on-answers\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:885:            [state text] (repl/recheck-on-answers state)]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:888:        (let [[state text] (repl/recheck-on-answers state)]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:895:            state (nth (iterate #(first (repl/recheck-on-answers %)) state) 3)]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:907:            [state _] (repl/recheck-on-answers state)\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:908:            [state _] (repl/recheck-on-answers state)]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:913:            [state' text] (repl/recheck-on-answers state)]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:928:      (let [[state' text'] (repl/recheck-on-load-events\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:934:    (let [[state text] (repl/recheck-on-answers (answer-at! state (allow id)))]\ntest/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:1005:          [state text] (repl/recheck-on-answers (answer-at! state (allow id)))\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-12 14:00:00 GMT\nCoding-Agent: claude (fable-5-1)\n# Task: REVISE the admission-in-the-linker design (round 2; read-only Architect)\nYour design: collab/1792260000000-architect-admission-in-linker.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md. Codex review (REJECT, four P1): collab/1792261000000-reviewer-admission-in-linker.findings.md (binding; read it whole). Original brief: collab/1792260000000-architect-admission-in-linker.prompt.md. FINAL MESSAGE = the complete revised design (Completed-GMT / Completed-Local first), self-contained.\nOWNER CORRECTION (verbatim, supersedes section 3 of your design and the \"importer\" key): \"all languages are compiled to the universal AST. The Universal AST is the programming language of yin.vm family of VMs. Whether a language is compiled from python, clojure, php, JS, java, yin.vm does not know nor does it care. yin.vm.linker should not care what the source language is either. There is no 'Clojure may use this module, Python may not' because at the vm level and the code linking level, there is only the universal AST and its projection a semantic datoms/tuples.\" So: DELETE the `:yin.link/importer` = frontend `[id revision]` key and the whole cross-language-by-frontend idea (AL-3 as written); no language, frontend or [id revision] in any linker datum. The admission question concerns principals (signing keys), addresses (A) and names; the \"who is asking\" subject is a COMPOSITION-OWNED context supplied to the interpreter (the existing `(verify decision context question)` context argument: the capability holder, e.g. the session's principal or a token holder), never a language. A published module is AST at an address; any frontend can import it if the holder's policy admits that principal/address. Registry reuse between frontends is not a linker security question; frontend runtime-state isolation (ruling 18, Python's py.rt cells) is a frontend/session concern outside the linker: say so briefly and do not design it here.\nFIX these codex findings: (1) the false claim that dao.jing.content.driver requires yin.repl.link/admission (the dependency runs the other way: yin.repl.link requires the driver); keep the move's justification on the two verified consumers (test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc, test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc) and the actual request-serving semantics; add test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:12 to the consumer inventory and the store_write_audit_test allowlist (test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj ~331); (2) the exposure statement: with the importer key gone, state exactly that admission follows the registry and its installation-family inheritance (engine ~1289-1307, 1396-1403, module.cljc ~552-554), is about principal+address+holder context, and is language-blind; delete \"never crosses a task boundary\"; say what \"untrust is not retroactive\" means; (3) the tick-to-VM handoff: specify precisely how the progress/response of one `round` reaches the waiting VM (the tick retains the round's successor and passes its response/progress into the pending driver, which runs the VM once before requiring another round to report progress; or the pending driver performs the tick's round itself): pick one, with acceptance: external allow arrives after the initial drive stopped; the tick's round delivers the response; no further question, input line, load event or answer needed; also a decision snapshot becoming available after parking; preserve one bounded drain per round and carry the successor before any raising VM run; (4) AL-1: make it a pure namespace relocation preserving the callable API and the session topology (including a note on `composition`/`serve` names), and put the API/topology reduction (`make`, `round`, one `:linker` value, the dht-only pair) in AL-2; full consumer inventory of require forms; update the store-write allowlist; regenerate renamed Dart namespaces and `rm -rf test/cljd-out` before glob-based runs; replace the literal empty grep by a namespace-dependency check that excludes docs and datum vocabulary (`:yin.repl/root`, error keywords); (5) AL-2's lexical assertion: absence of REPL-owned admission protocol state, drain/judge/serve calls and admission-specific hooks; configuration plumbing and display text allowed; restate the complete gate ladder G0-G4 (quick at landing, slow at phase boundaries) from docs/agents/build-n-test.md and add dao.jing selection if its files are edited. Also read the rest of codex's findings (Q4 placement note about link-install; the importer-key validators are now moot).\nSlices after the correction: AD-2 (in flight), AL-0 docs, AL-1 relocation, AL-2 REPL reduction + handoff, AL-3 becomes the subject/context plumbing (what composition supplies as holder context; trust commands as configuration of the in-process decision) , AL-4 trust commands: re-slice sensibly; the pinned-dependency discharge fix with L-d stays. Constraints: A is the only code identity; dao.stream P2P no privileged node; fetch has no deadline; no capability vocabulary in the linker; register-VM cutover independence. State unverified facts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
