{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,60p' src/dev/subsystems.edn; sed -n '1038,1065p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '30,65p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; sed -n '10,38p' test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; sed -n '15,35p' test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc; sed -n '1,40p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc; sed -n '18,40p' test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc; sed -n '22,42p' test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc; sed -n '20,42p' test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc; sed -n '26,44p' test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc; rg -n 'dependency-bindings|dependency-pin-mismatch|fetch|deadline' src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc; sed -n '18,25p' src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj; rg -n 'ruling 19|19\\\\.|trust.*safety|admission' docs/design/yang.antlr.md | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":";; Canonical Subsystems Definition for datom.world\n;; Longest-prefix match over Clojure/ClojureScript/ClojureDart namespaces.\n;; See docs/design/test.subsystems.md for architectural invariants and gate ladder.\n\n{:subsystems\n [;; Layer 0: Storage, Stream & Core Data Foundations\n  {:name \"dao.stream\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.stream\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.jing\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.jing\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.data\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.data\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.base\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.await\" \"dao.lease\" \"dao.pretty\" \"dao.datom\" \"dao.test-slow\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  ;; Layer 1: Space, GUI & Graphics\n  {:name \"dao.space\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.space\"]\n   :layer 1}\n\n  {:name \"dao.gui\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.gui\"]\n   :layer 1}\n\n  {:name \"dao.postgraphics\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.postgraphics\"]\n   :layer 1}\n\n  ;; Layer 2: Virtual Machines & Execution\n  {:name \"yin.vm.ucf\"\n   :prefixes [\"yin.vm.ucf\"]\n   :layer 2}\n\n  {:name \"yin.vm\"\n   :prefixes [\"yin.vm\"]\n   :layer 2}\n\n  ;; Layer 3: Languages & Repl\n  {:name \"yin.repl\"\n   :prefixes [\"yin.repl\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  {:name \"yang.python\"\n   :prefixes [\"yang.python\" \"yang.antlr\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  {:name \"yang.base\"\n   :prefixes [\"yang.clojure\" \"yang.php\" \"yang.frontend\" \"yang.safepoint\"\n              \"yang.stage\" \"yang.tails\" \"yang.io\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  ;; Layer 4: Demos & World Applications\n  {:name \"demo\"\n   the caller only prints.\"\n  [state server now]\n  (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n        state (custody-control-step (assoc state :repl repl))]\n    (cond\n      (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n      [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server dht-lines]\n\n      (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n      [state server dht-lines]\n\n      :else\n      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-load-events (:repl state) events)\n            [repl answered] (shell/recheck-on-answers repl)\n            dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n                        (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked)\n                        (seq answered) (conj answered))\n            state (assoc state :repl repl)\n            stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n            stepped (if (:running? stepped)\n                      (custody-program-step stepped)\n                      (custody-stop stepped))\n            [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n            server' (when server\n                      (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n                                  now))\n            [server-entries server''] (if server'\n                                        (serve/take-outbox server')\n   L-e, again with no install child and no output.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.datom :as datom]\n    [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    [dao.jing.dht.mesh :as mesh]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    [dao.space.dht-test :as dht-test]\n    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    [yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture :as fixture]\n    [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yin.repl.admission :as admission]\n    [yin.repl.link :as link]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The fast tests: publication order, cycles, admission\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private stand-in-address\n  \"A stand-in `py` address: a refused publication never reads it.\"\n  :test/address)\n\n\n(defn- unit\n  [nm pk]\n  {:name nm, :packet pk, :package? false})\n\n\n   A linked run builds the program's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately\n   until the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker\n   is not a backend here: its link of `py` is refused `:undeclared-free`\n   until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    [yin.repl.link :as link]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as dl]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as rc]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n  \"The ordinary Python composition's `integer` limits.\"\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test :as portable]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\n    [yin.repl.link :as link]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def ^:private limits\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n            [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n            [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\n            [yin.repl.link :as link]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as rc]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn :as db]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dc]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-resolve :as dr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as dl]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-contract-test :as contract]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus :refer [lit v lam app tail if-node def! resume]]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.derive :as derive]))\n\n\n(def worked-example\n  \"`((fn [x] (+ x 1)) 10)`, the same worked example `yin.vm.linearize-test`\n   uses -- a simple program with no duplicate parameters, no free-variable\n   surprises beyond the primitive `+`, and one level of closure nesting.\"\n  (app (lam '[x] (tail (app (v '+) (v 'x) (lit 1)))) (lit 10)))\n\n\n(def duplicate-param\n            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n            [yin.repl.link :as link]\n            [yin.repl.net-fixture :as fixture]\n            [yin.repl.serve :as serve]\n            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; An injected host listener\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- endpoint!\n  ([] (endpoint! {}))\n  ([extra]\n   (let [h (fixture/host)]\n     {:host h\n      :endpoint (serve/serve! (merge {:bind-port 8080\n                                      :host (:adapter h)}\n                                     extra))})))\n\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    [yang.python.antlr.c3-programs :refer [asg call e ex lit op st tc tx vr]]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test :refer [packet]]\n    [yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.repl]\n    #?@(:cljd [] :clj [[yang.python.antlr.parser :as parser]\n                       [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as probe]])\n    [yin.repl :as repl]\n    [yin.repl.frontends :as frontends]\n    [yin.repl.link :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Precompiled packets\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- module\n  [& stmts]\n  (packet (-> [:file_input] (into stmts) (conj [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]))))\n\n   non-evaluating reader, so quoted names are spelled `(quote ...)`.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.link :as link]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-vm-contract-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; AST helpers and the module corpora\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as rc]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.link :as link]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; AST helpers\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc:10:   owner and fetches each blob the walk answers missing.  A link runs\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc:92:   the node.  `dao.space.dht/step` fetches what is missing.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc:302:(defn dependency-bindings\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:32:   step fetches.  A failed load is refused in its section 9 shape and\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:87:   two the manifest flow fetches internally.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:365:      (let [bindings (linker.dht/dependency-bindings node authority address)\n   this handle. JVM-only, so the whole namespace is plain Clojure.\"\n\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.content.step :as step]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n\n\n(def default-request-timeout-ms\n1653:code that no site mark reaches, and it enforces admission in every\n1979:integration gate, profile admission and the sequence-size limit). C1\n2068:it, and a composition without it is refused at admission. Admission is\n2141:  left shift of a nonzero operand passes result-size admission first.\n2617:pin, heap and closure round trips, and continuation admission and\n2833:deferred dependency admission with statement-time resolution: check\n2838:address verification or admission. Until then an absent dependency\n3035:its tests (ruling 19), verifying closure origin and store ownership\n3039:dependency-pin checks, primitive and effect admission, and working\n3044:which principals' modules a session admits is the admission\n3072:|      | admission (ruling 8)                                |                 |\n3074:| L-e  | D7 slice B, the origin and store check (ruling 19)  | Exposure of     |\n3108:| I3    | Publication and DHT import; admission per `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5 |\n3224:  Which principals' modules an import admits is the admission stream's\n3875:  have landed (`cf6ed9ad`, and `e2a80eef` with generator admission against\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
